        "raw_score": 5.910904291297569,
        "source": "kg"
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_14",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Gian Giacomo Medici was the brother of Giovanni Angelo Medici, who was later to be elected Pope as Pius IV. They were scions of an impoverished though patrician family of Milan not connected with the Medici of Florence, in spite of the Medici heraldic \"palle\" appearing in the contemporary engraving (\"illustration\"): thus the nickname \"Il Medeghino\", the \"little Medici\".",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.8971713871913364,
      "temperature": 0.8971713871913364,
      "expanded": false,
      "visit_count": 0,
